# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# SDR captures: ELRS Find sweeps save to captures/elrs_find_*/. The WHOLE capture
# folder is SYNCED via git — raw IQ (.complex8/.cf32/.iq) AND the per-channel
# metadata (.meta.txt/.json/manifest.json) — so the other session gets every
# channel's samples to deep-analyze. The pre-push hook (scripts/git/pre-push)
# auto-commits captures/ on every `git push`, so new sweeps upload with no manual
# `git add`. Everything that looks like a stray capture OUTSIDE captures/ stays
# ignored (the blanket *.complex8 etc. below), and the `!captures/**` lines
# re-include the capture subtree.
#   NOTE: a full 80-ch sweep is ~160 MB, and git keeps every version forever, so
#   this grows .git over time. To reclaim it later: delete dead captures (they
#   leave history) then do a coordinated `git filter-repo` + re-clone.
*.iq
*.complex8
*.cf32
*.jsonl
!captures/
!captures/**/
!captures/**/*.complex8
!captures/**/*.cf32
!captures/**/*.iq
!captures/**/*.meta.txt
!captures/**/*.json
!captures/**/manifest.json

# C++ build artifacts (cpp/build.sh produces these)
cpp/elrs_intercept
cpp/tests/test_elrs_decode
cpp/tests/test_lora_demod
cpp/test_elrs_decode
cpp/test_lora_demod
cpp/*.bin
cpp/*.o

# Tarballs / archives — never commit
*.tgz
*.tar.gz

# Scan output (regenerated)
scan.jsonl
